## Pages

- **Overview** (`pages/overview.py`): starter page with sample numbers; replace it with your real pages.

## Queries

- `queries/example_metric.sql`: placeholder; repoint `YOUR_TABLE` at a real object in an allowed schema
  (the review window in `sql_review/index.yaml` reads it too). Or, once real queries exist, delete the
  query and its `example_metric` entry in `sql_review/index.yaml`, then run
  `streamsnow sql-review generate {{ app_slug }}`, which removes the rendered `sql_review/01_overview.sql`.
  `validate-app` fails while any app file still reads `YOUR_TABLE`.

## SQL review

`sql_review/` holds one runnable SQL file per page, generated from `sql_review/index.yaml`; its
`AGENTS.md` has the rules. Each metric a page shows is listed there and marked in the page with
`review_value("<key>", value)`.

## Data notes

Facts about the data this app reads that a reviewer needs and the SQL does not say: grain (one row
per what), metric definitions, known quirks and exclusions, freshness (when sources load).
Keep them here, in one place; `sql_review/` points to this section.

